# ⚙️ MLOps (Machine Learning Operations) – SMIT Data Science & AI Course

Welcome to the **MLOps** module of the **Saylani Mass IT Training (SMIT) Data Science & Artificial Intelligence** program!

This directory focuses on taking machine learning models out of Jupyter Notebooks and turning them into reliable, automated, production-grade applications. It covers model deployment, pipeline orchestration, experiment tracking, version control, containerization, and continuous integration/continuous delivery (CI/CD) for machine learning systems.

---

## 📂 Module Topics & Architecture

| Topic / Focus Area | Description | Key Tools & Frameworks |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **01. Model Packaging & API Serving** | Converting trained models into scalable web microservices (REST/gRPC APIs) | `FastAPI`, `Flask`, `Uvicorn` |
| **02. Containerization** | Packaging models, dependencies, and runtimes into lightweight, portable environments | `Docker`, `Docker Compose` |
| **03. Experiment Tracking & Registry** | Logging parameters, metrics, artifacts, and managing model versioning | `MLflow`, `DVC` |
| **04. Data & Pipeline Versioning** | Versioning datasets, data pipelines, and reproducible model training steps | `DVC` (Data Version Control), `Git` |
| **05. CI/CD for Machine Learning** | Automating testing, building, and deploying ML models on code updates | `GitHub Actions` |
| **06. Model Monitoring & Logging** | Tracking performance drift, data drift, payload logging, and model health in production | `Evidently AI`, `Prometheus` |

---

## 🛠️ Typical Project Layout

```text
MLOPs/
├── app/
│   ├── main.py             # FastAPI / Flask application entrypoint
│   ├── predict.py          # Inference script
│   └── utils.py            # Preprocessing & helper functions
├── models/
│   └── model_v1.pkl        # Serialized production model artifact
├── tests/
│   └── test_api.py         # Unit & integration tests
├── Dockerfile              # Containerization instructions
├── docker-compose.yml      # Multi-container setup (API + Tracking server)
├── requirements.txt        # Python dependencies
└── README.md
